WEBVTT

00:00:00.332 --> 00:00:02.660
Your coding agent finished the change.

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:12.474
Before you merge, what deserves a closer look? Revu gives you a local workspace to inspect the diff, investigate review signals, and prepare clear feedback.

00:00:14.533 --> 00:00:16.054
Start with a local scan.

00:00:16.054 --> 00:00:24.587
In this deliberately flawed sample, Revu flags a removed tenant filter, lost payment idempotency, and a changed function contract.

00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:27.960
Every flag includes evidence and verification steps.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.664
These are signals to investigate, not proof of a defect.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.099
The function's argument order changed.

00:00:36.099 --> 00:00:40.196
Find related callers and tests to inspect code outside the patch.

00:00:40.196 --> 00:00:43.780
This is a bounded name search, not a semantic call graph.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:48.582
Here, an unchanged caller still passes the arguments in the previous order.

00:00:50.646 --> 00:00:53.441
Record a needs fix decision with a concrete reason.

00:00:53.441 --> 00:00:56.515
Revu keeps that evidence with the current code snapshot.

00:00:56.515 --> 00:01:04.453
The review summary separates requested fixes from unreviewed signals and outstanding checks, then prepares a focused fix brief for your agent.

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:09.048
Advanced features helps prepare the handoff.

00:01:09.048 --> 00:01:13.017
Choose the changed files and explicitly select project instructions.

00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:18.704
Diff hunks and current reviewer notes are batched by file, with stable instructions at the start.

00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:22.317
Inspect the complete prompt before copying or downloading it.

00:01:24.361 --> 00:01:28.426
Compare compact and full-file estimates, then set a handoff budget.

00:01:28.426 --> 00:01:32.861
Revu warns near the limit and blocks export when the estimate reaches it.

00:01:32.861 --> 00:01:37.481
These are rough estimates, not provider billing or a daily spending control.

00:01:37.481 --> 00:01:39.268
Savings depend on the change.

00:01:41.308 --> 00:01:44.885
Use Policy studio to test a team rule against sample code.

00:01:44.885 --> 00:01:48.399
Review the match, its impact, and the verification steps.

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:52.540
Download the validated configuration and add it to your repository.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:57.874
You can also inspect AI primitives, navigate symbols, and prepare release checklists.

00:01:59.924 --> 00:02:02.498
Try Revu's free Windows developer preview.

00:02:02.498 --> 00:02:05.699
It runs locally and includes this sample repository.

00:02:05.699 --> 00:02:10.281
This is an unsigned alpha, with heuristic checks and manual agent handoff.

00:02:10.281 --> 00:02:15.491
Share useful findings and false positives on GitHub to help shape the next release.
